{#
  T-4.23 — the shoppable video carousel.

  | Variable                      | Type    | Description                       |
  |-------------------------------|---------|-----------------------------------|
  | component.items[].cover       | string  | The still the page actually shows |
  | component.items[].alt         | ?string | Empty means decorative            |
  | component.items[].embed_url   | string  | YouTube, TikTok or Instagram      |
  | component.items[].poster      | ?string | Who posted it                     |
  | component.items[].product_id  | ?string | Resolved at runtime, never stored |
  | position                      | int     | Sorting number, from zero         |

  THE CARRIER IS T-4.21'S. `salla-slider type="carousel" centered` already draws
  a centred slide with its neighbours partly visible, and the progress-bar
  pagination is the same `slider-config` merge — so this section adds no third
  slider and no third indicator.

  NOTHING THIRD-PARTY LOADS UNTIL THE VIEWER ASKS, which is an acceptance
  criterion and both a performance and a privacy one. What renders is the
  merchant's cover image and a play control; the iframe is created on activation
  by `partials/video-carousel.js`. **`lite-youtube-embed` is bundled and was the
  obvious candidate — it is YouTube-only**, and the owner's ruling covers TikTok
  and Instagram too, so one generic façade serves all three rather than one
  library plus a special case.

  THE PLAY BUTTON IS AN ADDITION TO THE ARTBOARD, and a necessary one. The
  artboard's slides are screenshots of posts, which show no play control because
  they are pictures of a video player. A façade needs something to ask **with**:
  without a control there is nothing to press, nothing to reach by keyboard, and
  nothing to name. Recorded in /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  THE PRODUCT LINE IS RESOLVED FROM ITS ID, exactly as the hotspot pill is, and
  through the same `partials/product-runtime` helpers. A renamed or repriced
  product needs no edit here.
#}
{% set video_items = component.items|default([]) %}

{% if video_items|length %}
    <section data-testid="store-home-video-carousel" class="s-block video-carousel container">
        <div class="s-block__panel">
            <salla-slider
                type="carousel"
                class="video-carousel__slider"
                centered
                pagination
                slider-config='{"pagination":{"el":"#video-{{ position }}-slider .swiper-pagination","type":"progressbar","clickable":false}}'
                id="video-{{ position }}-slider">
                <div slot="items">
                    {% for item in video_items %}
                        <div class="swiper-slide video-carousel__slide">
                            <div class="video-carousel__frame"
                                 data-video-slide
                                 data-embed-url="{{ item.embed_url }}">
                                <img class="video-carousel__cover"
                                     src="{{ item.cover }}"
                                     alt="{{ item.alt|default('') }}"
                                     width="900"
                                     height="1011"
                                     loading="lazy"
                                     decoding="async">

                                {% if item.poster %}
                                    {# The artboard bakes the poster's identity into the
                                       screenshot. A merchant's own still will not have
                                       it, so it is rendered — as text, never as a
                                       scraped avatar. #}
                                    <p class="video-carousel__poster"><bdi>{{ item.poster }}</bdi></p>
                                {% endif %}

                                {% if item.embed_url %}
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="video-carousel__play"
                                            data-video-play
                                            aria-label="{{ item.poster
                                                ? trans('theme.video.play_named', { name: item.poster })
                                                : trans('theme.video.play') }}">
                                        {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'play', size: 'xl' } only %}
                                    </button>
                                {% endif %}
                            </div>

                            {# Filled by partials/video-carousel.js from the product id,
                               and hidden until then so a failed lookup leaves no empty
                               row behind. Same contract as the hotspot pill. #}
                            {% if item.product_id %}
                                <div class="video-carousel__product"
                                     data-video-product
                                     data-product-id="{{ item.product_id }}"
                                     hidden></div>
                            {% endif %}
                        </div>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </salla-slider>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
